Friday interface (apps/ui)

Friday's mascot is an original character: a squishy cream creature — an egg
of a body with two rounded ears and a small tail, ink eyes and a blush — drawn
in code with the Canvas 2D API (src/mascot). The character's geometry,
colours, expressions and animations are Friday's own.

Some generic animation techniques in src/mascot were learned from the
MIT-licensed source code of the project "coucou"
(https://github.com/Louis-CFM/coucou):

  - spring smoothing: damped springs integrated in fixed sub-steps of
    1/240 s, frame-rate-independent smoothing x += (t - x)(1 - c^dt), and
    channel tweens whose keys start from the previous key's target;
  - eye tracking: the cursor's offset from the face, clamped, smoothed, and
    projected as features on a curved surface;
  - an on-demand frame loop that stops when nothing moves, randomised blinks,
    and particles positioned from their age with a ramped alpha.

No names, characters, artwork, icons, expressions, geometry or colours are
taken from that project. Its names and its character are reserved by their
author and are not used by Friday.

